 "description": "Six batch jobs write data another job reads. WRTA and WRTB both write MASTER, so they are bound and form a coupled group. WRTE and WRTF write different datasets but both call PGMX, so they are bound by the shared program and form a second coupled group. WRTC writes OTHER and no other writer shares it. WRTD reads MASTER, which WRTA and WRTB write, and writes THIRD. A reader is ordered after a writer but is not bound to it, so WRTC and WRTD are the independent group and go first. Five read-only jobs read the outputs.",
